# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
#   1. Make a COPY of this file named exactly ".env" (not .env.example) in the
#      same folder as app.py.
#   2. Paste your real key into that .env file.
#   3. That's it — the app auto-loads .env on startup (via python-dotenv),
#      no need to `export` anything in your terminal.
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit your real .env file to GitHub. Keep committing
# THIS file (.env.example) with blank values, so others know what's needed
# without seeing your actual key. Add ".env" to your .gitignore.

# RECOMMENDED: Groq — free, no card required, very fast (good for live demos)
# 1. Sign up at https://console.groq.com
# 2. Create an API key
# 3. Paste it into your .env file (not this one)
GROQ_API_KEY=


# ALTERNATIVE: OpenAI — paid, needs billing set up
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# The system runs correctly with NEITHER key set (heuristic fallback mode) —
# setting one just upgrades schema mapping and explanations to use an LLM.
# If both are set, Groq is used first.

# Optional tuning overrides (defaults are set in src/config.py)
# AUTO_MATCH_THRESHOLD=90
# AMOUNT_TOLERANCE_PCT=0.5
# MAX_REASONABLE_DELAY_DAYS=5
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Optional: shared database for exception reviews (default: local SQLite file).
# Free options: Neon or Supabase. Paste the connection string they give you.
# VERITY_DB_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname
